- Sky and aerial perspective: Sébastien Hillaire, "A Scalable and Production Ready Sky and Atmosphere Rendering
  Technique", Eurographics Symposium on Rendering 2020. Also Eric Bruneton and Fabrice Neyret, "Precomputed
  Atmospheric Scattering", 2008, for the scattering constants.
- Optical depth through the curved atmosphere: Christian Schüler, "An Approximation to the Chapman Grazing-Incidence
  Function for Atmospheric Scattering", GPU Pro 3, 2012.
- Volumetric clouds, Perlin-Worley noise and the cloud shapes and lighting: Andrew Schneider and Nathan Vos, "The
  Real-time Volumetric Cloudscapes of Horizon: Zero Dawn", SIGGRAPH 2015 Advances in Real-Time Rendering. Also Andrew
  Schneider, "Nubis: Authoring Real-Time Volumetric Cloudscapes with the Decima Engine", SIGGRAPH 2017.
- Multiple scattering in clouds: Magnus Wrenninge, Chris Kulla and Viktor Lundqvist, "Oz: The Great and Volumetric",
  SIGGRAPH 2013 Talks.
- Phase function: L. G. Henyey and J. L. Greenstein, "Diffuse radiation in the galaxy", 1941.
- Tone mapping: the ACES filmic curve fit by Krzysztof Narkowicz, 2016.
